## What it is

A sci-fi action game focused on agile combat, cooperative missions, and building your collection of equipment.

## Is this your kind of game?

Consider Warframe if you enjoy cooperative action alongside a longer progression system. Before installing, look at how missions and equipment progression fit together so you can decide whether that structure suits your play time.

## Download and purchase

The base game is listed as free to play; optional purchases may be available. Use the official Steam button on this page to open the publisher's listing. Installation is handled by Steam; GameNews does not host installers or game files.

The Steam listing identifies a Warframe account requirement. Check the current account-linking instructions on the official store.

## What the Steam listing shows

Checked 23 November 2026. Steam lists Digital Extremes as both developer and publisher, with a Steam release date of 25 March 2013. The listing covers single-player, online co-op, and cross-platform multiplayer, with full controller support.

The minimum column asks for 64-bit Windows 7 (32-bit is not supported), an Intel Core i7 860, Intel Core i5 750, or AMD FX-4100, a DirectX 11 capable graphics card, 4 GB of memory, 75 GB of storage, and a broadband connection. Steam says the processor must support SSE 4.2, and that DirectX 12 needs Windows 10 20H2 or Windows 11. The listing says no Mac or Linux client is available.

## Sources and editorial basis

Product information checked against the [official Steam listing](https://store.steampowered.com/app/230410/?l=english) on 16 October 2026 and rechecked on 23 November 2026. Selected with reference to [Steam's most-played chart](https://store.steampowered.com/charts/mostplayed/). This is a researched profile, not a hands-on review or a search-volume ranking. Live prices, player counts, and performance scores are intentionally not quoted.
